$MDESC::Type = "CTF_HamstersMaps";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> Capture the Flag" @
         "\n<f1>Author: <f0> Hamster_of_Doom!" @
	 "\n<f1>Questions, Comments, Pity: <f0> rvr279@home.com" @	
 	 "\n<f1>ICQ: <f0> 25400277 <f1>AIM: <f0> Rover v1" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Map Version: <f0> 1.2" @
	 "\n<f1>Updates: <f0> http://members.home.net/rvr279/hamster" @
	 "\n<f1>Map Type: <f0> Server-Side" @
	 "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Larua" @
         "\n<f1>System: <f0> Mahkali" @
         "\n<f1>Gravity: <f0> Normal" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Clear" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Midday" @ 
         "\n<f1>Date: <f0> March 1st, 4025" @
         "\n<f1>Campaign: <f0> Brunt" @         
	 "\n<f1># of Captures to Victory: <f0> 6" @
	 "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
	 "\n<f1>Max # of Players: <f0> 30" @
	 "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> Listen up soldiers! As you know the fighting has been intense since the siege of our base near the capital of Opula Magnus began back in February. Both sides have paid a high price. During the Battle of Trident, we lost our main base on Larua when the enemy set off sequentially timed explosions. Thankfully, they lost their base too when the detonation triggered a massive earthquake that swallowed a good chunk of Opula Magnus and most of their encampment. Unfortunately, our reinforcements have still not arrived. They are having to fight through an enemy blockade in the outer asteroid rings of this system. The fleet commander, the fearless Captain Thomas Xelsiur himself has contacted me and ensured me that if our forces can hold out for another week, they will be able to reach this planet and provide us much needed relief. We have already scavenged the nearby terrain for every remaining scrap and entrenched ourselves for this final confrontation. But so has the enemy. Both our flags and those of the enemy lie in deep pits in the center of the entrenchments. If we can capture their flag 6 times, we will be able to ultimately secure this system once and for all!\n\nFailure is not an option.\n\nDISMISSED!\n\n<f1>Tips:\n<f0>The flags are hard to cap by 'drive-bys' unless stealth is used. If you are gaurding the flags, set up proper defenses.\nRemember, as in most maps, the best chance you have to capture the enemy flag is with teamwork!\n\n<f1>Version History<f0>\nVers 1.2\nUpdated contact info.\n\nVers. 1.1\nUpdated (.dsc) description file.\nChanged cap limit from default to 6.\n\n<f1>Thanks to:\n<f0>Shadow of Death and Tedaw for debuting my maps on their server!\nOmnipotent & others for their mapping tutorials.\nThe mapping community at large for inspiration, demonstration, and perspiration.\nAnd of course the team at Dynamix for Tribes!";